.PP
A color input: a box showing the color (like \fBGtkColorDialogButton\fR) that opens a \fBColorPicker\fR with an entry for the color code, in a popover or a dialog. See the module.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.TP
.B ColorInput::new(value: Hsva, text: &'a str, on_input: impl Fn(String) \-> M + 'a, on_change: impl Fn(Hsva) \-> M + 'a)
\fBtext\fR is what the entry in the picker shows (the app keeps it, so typing is not interrupted); \fBvalue\fR is the color. \fBon_input\fR gets the typed text, \fBon_change\fR a color picked with the controls: parse the text with \fBHsva::parse\fR and format a picked color with \fBHsva::format\fR.
